WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Simulated XYZ targets move through four LD6004 detection cuboids. Drop-lines
show height above the floor.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.001
Drag empty scene space to orbit. Icon buttons zoom the camera without changing
bounds.

3
00:00:10.001 --> 00:00:19.002
Click another cube. Drag faces to move X/Y and height, then a vertical edge to
resize X/Y. The height arrow clamps at the limit.

4
00:00:19.002 --> 00:00:21.884
Enter 4.2 metres. Apply uses staged writes.

5
00:00:21.884 --> 00:00:22.700
Apply is pending.

6
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.002
The simulated actual values now agree. The staged draft is confirmed.

7
00:00:25.002 --> 00:00:29.003
A further height edit stays local. Discard restores actual values, and Fit
adjusts the camera.

8
00:00:29.003 --> 00:00:35.004
Top view edits the same zone as a rectangle. Drag its centre to move and a
corner to resize.

9
00:00:35.004 --> 00:00:39.004
Pause freezes target motion while precise editing remains available. Resume
starts motion again.

10
00:00:39.004 --> 00:00:45.004
LD2450 has three 2D zones. Select Zone 3 and Apply to update its simulated
millimetre entities from metre bounds.

11
00:00:45.004 --> 00:00:51.005
LD6002B adds four interference areas. Select Interference 0 and resize its
height and X bound precisely with axis arrows.

12
00:00:51.005 --> 00:00:54.005
Reset clears local edits and restores the simulated sensor mapping. Try the
interactive demo.
